    "prompt": "Use case: stylized-concept. Paint 24 NEW Mindustry terrain floor tiles, refined clean bright Daoist Q hand-painted materials using two attached references as craftsmanship reference ONLY. NO UI, text, symbols, people, raised props or perspective. Requested2048×3072 portrait, exactly FOUR columns × SIX rows of square full-bleed material swatches without gutters, lines, borders or labels. Strict top-down FLAT GROUND. Each row FOUR different native variants of same material, uniform mean brightness/color and feature scale, distinct patterns no copied tiles. Even overhead daylight, no lighting gradient/vignette. Fine material texture, soft rounded broad planes, sparse accents and low-medium contrast; naturally tileable quiet edges, every cell opaque.\nRow1 BERYLLIC STONE: desaturated pale sage-jade gray rock, tiny beryl-green mineral grains, soft irregular chalky stone plates.\nRow2 DENSE RED STONE: dense dusty rust-red brick-colored natural rock with close irregular hairline fractures and subtle dark mottling, NOT manufactured bricks.\nRow3 RED STONE: lighter warm terracotta rosy stone ground with broad rounded natural plates, fine warm beige mineral veins.\nRow4 FERRIC STONE: muted warm iron-brown ocher rock with tiny rusty orange iron flecks and sparse shallow soft cracks.\nRow5 ROUGH RHYOLITE: muted purple-mauve gray rough volcanic ground, coarse rounded rocky grains and small shallow surface fissures, all flat.\nRow6 CARBON STONE: very dark blue charcoal-gray carbon-rich ground, flat broad smooth fractured plates with subtle blue-gray rims, no bright lava.\nPreserve sensible functional material identity; never simply recolor a shared crack drawing. Precisely24 fullbleed squares, no text.",
